  "question": {
    "text": "For the reaction, $\\mathbf{X}(s) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathbf{Y}(s)+\\mathbf{Z}(g)$, the plot of $\\ln \\frac{p_{\\mathbf{Z}}}{p^{\\theta}}$ versus $\\frac{10^{4}}{T}$ is given below (in solid line), where $p_{\\mathbf{Z}}$ is the pressure (in bar) of the gas $\\mathbf{Z}$ at temperature $T$ and $p^{\\theta}=1$ bar.<br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/O3KPX_MwSVyabCGPvfrP2UF_XRyrV8G6SZztjXaUK-4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>(Given, $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}(\\ln K)}{\\mathrm{d}\\left(\\frac{1}{T}\\right)}=-\\frac{\\Delta H^{\\theta}}{R}$, where the equilibrium constant, $K=\\frac{p_{z}}{p^{\\theta}}$ and the gas constant, $\\mathrm{R}=8.314 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ )<br><p>The value of standard enthalpy,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;(in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)&nbsp;for the given reaction is ___.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
